abstract: >-
  Privacy-KB is a local engine for United States federal, New York State and New York City
  privacy law. It answers which obligations apply as of a given date, with exemptions typed and
  preemption resolved; computes counterfactual exposure, date-window differences and element
  coverage against a source's own segmentation; produces reproducible artifacts including
  verifiable receipts and standing fact registers; and audits the citations in any answer,
  including answers it did not produce. Every provision is quoted verbatim from a stored primary
  source and anchored to the SHA-256 of the bytes it was verified against, so any quotation can be
  checked. No language model participates in the applicability decision. The design reports the
  boundary of what it can establish — coverage gaps, element shortfall, and differences it cannot
  attribute to a dated legal event are returned with the answer rather than omitted from it.
